.TH CHTTPCLI_CONSTRUCT_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_construct_scoped \- declare and initialize a chttpcli handle that the library destroys automatically
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

chttpcli_construct_scoped(name)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro joins chttpcli_declare_scoped and the call to
ccol_create_chttpclient. It declares name with the cleanup attribute
of GCC. It then calls ccol_create_chttpclient and sets name. The
library destroys the client automatically when name leaves the scope.
If the creation fails, the macro calls ccol_fatal_err() and does not
return.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name     The identifier of the new handle variable.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_construct (3),
.BR chttpcli_declare_scoped (3)
